---
import "../styles.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-AU">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Snake Arena</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <nav aria-label="site">
      <a href="/">Snake Arena</a>
      <a href="/play/">Play</a>
      <a href="/leaderboard/">Leaderboard</a>
      <a href="/readme/">About</a>
    </nav>
    <main>
      <h1>Snake Arena</h1>
      <p>
        A grid-based Snake game, playable right now with no sign-up. This first
        version is solo: you against the wall, your own tail, and the
        leaderboard. A later version adds other snakes on the same board at
        the same time — the rules here are already built to grow into that.
      </p>
      <div class="panel">
        <h2>How to play</h2>
        <p>
          Steer with the arrow keys or <kbd>W</kbd> <kbd>A</kbd> <kbd>S</kbd>
          <kbd>D</kbd>. Eat the amber dot to grow and score; hitting a wall or
          your own tail ends the game. Press Restart to go again.
        </p>
        <a class="button primary" href="/play/">Play now</a>
      </div>
      <p>
        Every finished game is recorded under an anonymous player name the
        server assigns you (something like <em>Player A7F3</em>) — no account,
        no email, just enough identity to put your run on the
        <a href="/leaderboard/">leaderboard</a>.
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
